  "note": "Kozjak’s pale rockfill dam with its 302.80 m mapped crest road, circular overflow, white red-roof tower, intake rails and lower two-unit generating complex with ochre walls, red gabled roofs and outdoor electrical equipment. Signed datum 468 m. The exterior uses an approximate 474.4 m crest and 348.3 m foundation for the stated 126.1 m dam height. The operator gives 459 m maximum operating pool and 432 m minimum. The standard viewer samples 468.65 m headwater and 361.58 m in the lower pool. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
